WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
Vive le Front National!

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:02.860
Vive la République!

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.080
Vive la France!

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.960
Marine Le Pen is a leading candidate in the
French presidential race.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.220
The first round of voting is on April 23rd,

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.030
which will narrow the field to two

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.240
for a runoff election on May 7.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:23.120
Marine Le Pen is a far-right candidate and
represents the “Front National”,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.750
The National Front, which is the far-right party.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.300
The National Front has existed for a little
over forty years and Marine Le Pen

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.440
has been running the party since January 2011.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.200
Marine Le Pen is the daughter of the founder
of the National Front: Jean-Marie Le Pen.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.990
He founded it in the early 1970s and it was
considered a pretty racist anti-Semitic party

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.420
and always very marginalized.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.420
The party was seen as anti-Semitic in large part

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.840
because her father had often minimized the Holocaust.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:07.150
But Marine has distanced herself from her
father since 2015.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:11.180
In part, that’s because she has tried to
change the message of the party

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.539
and change the branding of the party.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:18.560
I excluded from the National Front my very own father.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.300
We could not tolerate words, unacceptable words,

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.920
that would lead to a caricature of our movement.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.400
By removing her father, Le Pen hoped to move
the party away from anti-Semitism,

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.600
but a recent comment has undercut those efforts.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:43.360
Speaking to the press, Marine Le Pen denied
that France was responsible for the Vel d’Hiv roundup,

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.880
which took place when French
authorities arrested Jews and brought them

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.700
to the Vélodrome d’Hiver indoor cycling track in Paris

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.680
for eventual delivery to Nazi concentration camps.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.259
She said this despite the fact that French
president Jacques Chirac formally acknowledged

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:05.659
guilt on behalf of the French state in 1995.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:11.280
By questioning French culpability in the Holocaust,
her comments have reopened old wounds.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.240
But for the time being,

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.140
Le Pen remains a leading contender,

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.700
as she has been throughout the campaign,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.720
and that’s largely due to her successful efforts to rebrand the National Front.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.840
Instead of being seen as anti-Semites, Le
Pen has worked to portray the party

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.180
as protectors of French identity and French values.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:49.760
Her big thing is about France for the French,
which gets into some of her policies, which

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:54.620
actually we would perceive as racist or xenophobic
but she sees them

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.280
as returning to a sort of mythical France.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.870
In a way, it reminds us a little bit of Trump.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:05.460
The forgotten men and women of our country
will be forgotten no longer.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.280
I am very happy about the election of Donald
Trump.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:15.200
I think that The United States will once again
regain its former image in the world,

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.420
which had become very damaged.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.780
To Marine Le Pen, there is a certain French
culture that should be upheld and that

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.300
that’s being lost in the tide of globalization.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.280
She’s particularly anti-globalization.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.780
She’s against The European Union and she
would like to radically reduce the number of immigrants.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.480
We are not going to welcome any more people.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.480
Stop!

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.580
We are full up!

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:42.680
During the 2015 refugee crisis, asylum seekers
fled to Europe from North Africa and the Middle East,

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.460
eventually landing in places like Calais, France,

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:48.840
home to a notorious refugee camp called “The Jungle”.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.700
Many Europeans felt overwhelmed by the sudden
influx

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.880
and Marine Le Pen seized the opportunity to elevate her nationalist platform.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:02.460
France didn’t absorb the same numbers of
people as Germany did or parts of Northern Europe.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:06.980
But, at the same time, there was a sense that
it was out of control: that Europe did not

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.520
know how to control its borders.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:31.300
Even though it was not connected, having the
attacks in Paris in the fall of 2015, and

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:38.240
then again in the summer of 2016 in Nice,
exacerbated a sense of a changing Europe.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.620
…reports are coming in of an attack…

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.500
…a shooting in central Paris…

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.690
…hearing at least twenty shots and seeing
more than fifteen dead…

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:50.340
…two young men, no older than twenty-five,
with Kalashnikovs…

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:56.720
The fear of attacks, the actuality of attacks,
tend to bolster support for closing borders,

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.700
closing down the immigration policies and

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.400
turning an eye on the community that people feel is at fault.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.700
While many leaders carefully avoided making
any assumptions about the perpetrators…

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:12.479
I don’t want to speculate at this point,
in terms of who was responsible for this.

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:15.210
…Marine Le Pen was quick to point the finger.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.900
Speaking on the floor of The European Parliament
shortly after the attacks,

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.640
she forcefully blamed Islamic fundamentalism for the tragedy in Paris.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.659
In 2010, France was home to nearly five million Muslims.

00:05:39.659 --> 00:05:44.830
Over a million more than The United States,
a country nearly five times the size of France.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:49.270
And many French Muslims are perceived as far
more religious than they are French.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:53.700
In part, that is due to the very visual issue
of the veil in public space.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.999
An issue that has been under debate in France
for over twenty-five years.

00:05:57.999 --> 00:06:03.939
Right now, as of 2004, it’s not allowed
in public schools, but they’ve stopped short

00:06:03.939 --> 00:06:08.080
of banning it in the street because that’s
seen as a personal liberties scenario, right?

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.020
Marine Le Pen would like to ban it in general.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.220
By setting classic liberal ideals against
Islamic fundamentalism,

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:34.879
Marine Le Pen promotes French nationalism by claiming she is protecting French identity.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:39.120
Similarly, she has framed globalization as
a threat to French values.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:54.200
Marine Le Pen has said she will hold a referendum
to pull France out of the EU.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.660
She would like to ask for a “Frexit”,
as we just had a Brexit.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.220
She would like a return to a sovereign currency

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:05.740
and she very much would like to return to a France of a different era.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:14.440
If France was to be able to be actually removed it would

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.840
be the end of the European experiment as we know it.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.400
Vive la République!

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.220
Vive la France!

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:24.340
As the National Front’s poll numbers have
risen over the past decade,

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:28.400
the rhetoric of other political candidates has begun to shift to the right.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:33.200
The parties to the center-right begin to adopt
a number of her ideas.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.480
Even if she doesn’t succeed, there is a
conversation taking place

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:40.800
that is much, much more skeptical of immigration.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:47.900
Now it has become radicalized and tinged with
this sort of anti-Islam Islamophobia space, as well.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.960
The real question is: do European nations,

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:59.020
are they nimble enough to move into a space of multiculturalism and is that what they want?

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.580
And one of the things that Marine Le Pen will say is,

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.140
“This is not a battle for an election,

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:09.880
this is a battle between globalization and patriotism.”

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:15.080
So, she sets it up as the idea that one is
not a patriot unless one buys into the idea

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:19.920
of a very specific type of France, which a
lot of people would see themselves left out of.

